# Purpose-based repository organization
Workstream-ID: lea-39
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/39
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed bounded repository organization request
Status: DONE
Milestone: Make source, guides, assets and development tools easier to navigate
Dependencies: lea-38

## Purpose
Reduce repository clutter without changing application behavior or relocating
existing private workspaces. Group guides, documentation assets, tests and
build/media utilities by purpose, with concise navigation and current references.

## Tasks
- [x] Inventory path-sensitive resources, current changes and protected runtimes.
- [x] Group documentation, assets, tests and build/media tooling.
- [x] Update navigation, resource loading, packaging and development commands.
- [x] Verify preservation, test discovery, resource paths and affected regressions.
- [x] Maintain the scoped issue, Project item and persistent backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Documentation has clear getting-started, guides, architecture and development sections.
- [x] Branding and screenshots have dedicated asset directories.
- [x] Tests and development tools are grouped by their responsibility.
- [x] Application launch commands, package imports and workspace locations stay compatible.
- [x] Source and frozen tutorial/icon resources use consistent existing files.
- [x] Earlier dirty work and original media survive the moves.
- [x] Historical workstreams, private inputs and independent applications remain intact.
- [x] One scoped issue-backed Project item/backlink preserves all 38 predecessors.
- [x] No commit, push, release, installation, live action or automation activation occurs.

## Completion evidence
Move 117 files into purpose-based documentation, asset, test and tool groups.
Add concise documentation, repository-layout, test and tool navigation.
Update source/frozen branding and tutorial resources, helper imports and
Windows workflow command paths; preserve its activation and permission policy.

Collect all 1,012 tests successfully; pass 290 affected desktop/tooling cases.
Ruff and Black pass; mypy passes 74 source files. Check 290 relative references
across 29 live documents with no introduced broken references. Three existing
run-guide fragment warnings remain attributed to the baseline.

All six harmless version/help probes pass, including the installed CLI entry
point and moved Windows/media tools. Correct the private probe's Windows
decoding error with explicit UTF-8; no product encoding change is needed.
Import the legacy banner generator and verify its moved SVG target without
regenerating media. Source/frozen resource tests check existing bundle inputs.

Verify every move, 241 unchanged file byte/modification-time identities,
original HEAD/index, selected private metadata and all 38 predecessor mappings.
Protected dashboard process creation identities remain unchanged. Preserve
historical workstreams and reviewed public handoff bytes rather than rewriting
their historical citations. The issue backlink is persisted; completion
synchronization is limited to this workstream.

This is local structural/offline qualification, not a new Windows build,
publication, live LinkedIn qualification or human acceptance.

